WEBVTT

00:04.480 --> 00:05.730
We can handle them.

00:06.300 --> 00:10.110
We have seven people who can use Musik.

00:10.430 --> 00:11.150
Huh?

00:12.060 --> 00:13.690
Shouldn't there be one more?

00:13.690 --> 00:14.810
You're right.

00:17.650 --> 00:18.890
Moderato.

00:19.820 --> 00:20.950
Fine.

00:23.870 --> 00:26.210
Don't tell me that's...

00:24.540 --> 00:27.960
24: The World of Eight Sounds: Part 2

00:26.610 --> 00:28.300
Schu-san...

00:31.450 --> 00:32.340
Staccato?

00:38.840 --> 00:39.450
Huh?

00:39.860 --> 00:40.560
Senpai?

00:40.860 --> 00:44.280
What the hell are you doing?
We're in the middle of something!

00:44.280 --> 00:46.710
Get over here and help us, you oaf!

00:46.710 --> 00:48.060
Y-Yes, sir. Sorry, sir.

00:54.030 --> 00:55.610
We can handle them.

00:55.900 --> 01:02.290
We have seven people who can use Musik.

02:38.340 --> 02:40.180
Now, confess everything!

02:40.180 --> 02:41.670
I've been cheating!

02:41.670 --> 02:43.330
I've had my eyes done!

02:43.330 --> 02:45.970
I burned all of our revenue on horse races!

02:46.950 --> 02:48.620
That's it!

02:49.430 --> 02:52.650
Don't do half-assed cosplay!

02:55.440 --> 02:56.520
What's going on?

02:56.520 --> 02:57.620
Where am I?

02:57.620 --> 02:58.530
Let me out.

03:01.090 --> 03:02.530
Worship me.

03:03.240 --> 03:04.710
Cower before me.

03:05.230 --> 03:06.330
The sun.

03:06.330 --> 03:07.510
It's the sun.

03:07.510 --> 03:08.550
<i>Now!</i>

03:09.520 --> 03:11.120
Bąda-sama!

03:11.850 --> 03:14.380
They all look alike, all these Bach clones!

03:14.380 --> 03:16.980
Here they all come, I'm the top, though

03:16.980 --> 03:19.630
Stay away, you creepy hobgobs

03:19.630 --> 03:21.880
Don't get so excited over crappy knock-offs

03:22.360 --> 03:26.930
Hear my Musik of love and rebirth.

03:28.000 --> 03:28.550
Huh?

03:28.550 --> 03:29.060
What?

03:29.970 --> 03:31.760
Uh...

03:31.760 --> 03:32.730
Wait.

03:33.370 --> 03:34.200
Hey.

03:34.200 --> 03:36.400
S-S-Stop!

03:36.940 --> 03:38.430
Farewell.

03:38.430 --> 03:39.360
Goodbye.

03:39.540 --> 03:41.580
Y-You idiot.

03:41.580 --> 03:42.660
I love you.

03:42.660 --> 03:43.910
I love you!

03:44.200 --> 03:47.650
I love you, too!

03:51.950 --> 03:52.750
Man...

03:53.290 --> 03:55.450
These guys sure are nuts.

03:55.960 --> 03:57.630
This is insane.

03:58.670 --> 04:00.060
What were we doing?

04:04.040 --> 04:05.230
I'm bored of this.

04:05.230 --> 04:07.380
Do you think they care
if you're bored or not?

04:07.380 --> 04:08.850
But there's no end to them.

04:09.840 --> 04:11.980
He's right. We can't keep this up.

04:11.980 --> 04:13.060
All right, then.

04:14.230 --> 04:15.550
I'll finish them with this!

04:15.550 --> 04:16.560
Enough!

04:16.770 --> 04:20.250
But why are they coming our way?

04:20.250 --> 04:22.490
If they're Bach-sama rip-offs,

04:22.490 --> 04:25.360
they're influenced by Bach-sama's ideology.

04:25.960 --> 04:29.530
Their main goal is to storm this mansion

04:29.530 --> 04:32.120
and take the ClassicaLoids home.

04:33.330 --> 04:36.690
So all the world's Bach-alikes
are going to make their way here?

04:36.690 --> 04:37.750
No...

04:38.000 --> 04:39.730
Uh, hello?

04:39.730 --> 04:40.750
Is Kanae there?

04:41.850 --> 04:42.760
Dad?

04:43.120 --> 04:44.590
Hey, Kanae.

04:44.950 --> 04:47.720
Have you heard what's causing
this phenomenon right now?

04:49.340 --> 04:50.220
Roughly.

04:50.430 --> 04:52.610
That speeds things up, then.

04:52.610 --> 04:56.050
The device in question is
near the top of Mount Oomori,

04:56.050 --> 04:58.690
inside the Arkhe research facility.

04:59.050 --> 05:01.340
I tried to shut it down remotely,

05:01.340 --> 05:04.050
but I lost power, so I couldn't do it.

05:04.050 --> 05:04.950
So, Kanae,

05:05.260 --> 05:08.960
would you do me a favor and go
there yourself to turn it off?

05:08.960 --> 05:09.800
What?

05:09.800 --> 05:11.100
Why do I have to do it?

05:11.100 --> 05:11.950
Don't worry.

05:12.650 --> 05:14.500
You're a strong girl.

05:14.980 --> 05:16.350
Seriously...

05:16.350 --> 05:19.500
Uh-oh, my tablet's almost out of ba—

05:22.010 --> 05:24.600
That deadbeat jerk...

05:24.600 --> 05:25.860
Kanae-san!

05:25.860 --> 05:28.480
Please don't apply any more force.

05:28.480 --> 05:29.280
I'll crack.

05:29.280 --> 05:30.660
I'm creaking!

05:30.660 --> 05:33.260
So what's the plan, Kanae?

05:35.630 --> 05:39.980
You're a strong, kind girl, Kanae.

05:42.970 --> 05:44.130
I'll do it.

05:44.130 --> 05:45.490
I'm going to go turn off the device.

05:45.490 --> 05:46.200
Seriously?

05:46.610 --> 05:49.220
I decided that I'm going to protect this house.

05:50.910 --> 05:53.160
Can I get someone to help me?

05:53.650 --> 05:56.460
I'm going to the research
facility to stop the device.

05:56.460 --> 05:58.290
It might be dangerous, but...

05:58.290 --> 05:58.990
I'll go!

05:58.990 --> 06:00.730
That sounds at least somewhat interesting.

06:00.730 --> 06:02.470
Better than grinding zombies.

06:02.470 --> 06:03.790
Leave it to me, my little kitten.

06:03.790 --> 06:05.280
Let's go.

06:07.510 --> 06:08.580
Wait a second.

06:08.580 --> 06:10.890
What are we going to do about
the mansion if everyone goes?

06:11.100 --> 06:13.100
Sousuke will probably figure it out.

06:13.100 --> 06:14.260
Hell, no.

06:14.260 --> 06:15.340
Umm...

06:15.340 --> 06:16.270
Three.

06:16.270 --> 06:17.850
No, two people is enough.

06:17.850 --> 06:20.010
Everyone else stay behind
to protect the mansion.

06:20.930 --> 06:22.750
We won't have anywhere to live.

06:22.750 --> 06:24.050
Isn't that bad?

06:24.680 --> 06:26.580
All right, then.

06:26.580 --> 06:28.360
Let us play rock-paper-scissors, then.

06:28.760 --> 06:30.830
Rock, paper, scissors.

06:30.830 --> 06:32.790
Let's try again.

06:32.790 --> 06:33.550
Again.

06:33.760 --> 06:34.590
Again.

06:34.800 --> 06:35.630
Again.

06:35.840 --> 06:36.680
Again.

06:36.880 --> 06:37.660
Again.

06:37.900 --> 06:39.270
Yay!

06:39.270 --> 06:41.670
Fate has chosen me after all.

06:42.270 --> 06:43.290
Off we go.

06:50.850 --> 06:52.650
Be safe, Kanae.

06:52.650 --> 06:53.500
Yeah.

06:53.500 --> 06:55.260
Keep the mansion safe, guys.

07:06.660 --> 07:08.380
And they're gone.

07:08.380 --> 07:10.110
Well, then...

07:11.230 --> 07:14.400
Can we hold them off until
the device is shut down?

07:14.400 --> 07:15.800
We don't have a choice.

07:16.280 --> 07:18.610
To wait, too, is to love.

07:20.620 --> 07:22.380
Stay out of this, tool.

07:22.380 --> 07:24.280
You can't use Musik, can you?

07:24.280 --> 07:26.350
Don't get cocky.

07:26.350 --> 07:27.760
Sorry.

08:13.620 --> 08:16.450
It's finally time.

08:19.550 --> 08:22.510
Every human in the world becomes Bach-sama.

08:22.510 --> 08:25.070
And I, too, become Bach-sama.

08:25.920 --> 08:27.650
I'm so excited.

08:27.650 --> 08:29.600
A truly great existence.

08:29.600 --> 08:33.820
From this day forward, I'm going
to worship my body and myself.

08:34.500 --> 08:35.250
Now...

08:37.200 --> 08:38.890
No, I have to savor it.

08:38.890 --> 08:39.840
I know.

08:39.840 --> 08:42.450
I should take a picture with
my wig before I wear it.

08:43.840 --> 08:45.350
Octovas is damaged?

08:45.350 --> 08:46.180
Why?

08:46.560 --> 08:47.520
The Musik...

08:50.570 --> 08:52.240
Looks like it hasn't stopped.

08:52.820 --> 08:54.470
What's going on?

09:07.700 --> 09:09.650
Let's hurry to the so-called device.

09:11.370 --> 09:12.850
What is it now?

09:14.690 --> 09:15.650
It's them.

09:17.370 --> 09:19.230
The MitsuruLoid 2.0s...

09:19.230 --> 09:20.970
Why are they moving on their own?

09:21.530 --> 09:24.160
Actually, this works in my favor.

09:25.650 --> 09:27.820
Attention all MitsuruLoids.

09:27.820 --> 09:30.720
Find and dispatch the three intruders.

09:43.000 --> 09:44.520
They look just like us.

09:44.880 --> 09:48.380
So these are the robots
that look just like us.

09:49.390 --> 09:51.270
Out of my way!

09:53.330 --> 09:54.030
Musik!

09:57.690 --> 09:58.650
All right, then...

10:05.320 --> 10:07.120
Go away, look-alikes.

10:11.560 --> 10:13.710
You can even use Musik.

10:13.710 --> 10:16.630
Can you imagine how popular we'd be with
the chicks if we went drinking together?

10:17.010 --> 10:18.380
Pesky little robots...

10:19.490 --> 10:22.260
You'll never be worthy of imitating me.

10:28.000 --> 10:30.310
Have a coffee break.

10:47.150 --> 10:49.350
Looks like you weren't waterproof.

10:51.590 --> 10:53.540
Hey, how about this, then?

11:06.840 --> 11:07.760
Uh-oh.

11:07.760 --> 11:09.060
Are you broken?

11:09.840 --> 11:11.060
Wh-Why?

11:11.870 --> 11:14.400
They used Musik that wasn't
in their input data.

11:15.210 --> 11:17.810
They're more evolved than I thought.

11:19.130 --> 11:21.260
I need to repair the Octovas first.

11:22.900 --> 11:24.910
Y-You defeated them?

11:25.830 --> 11:26.410
I guess.

11:26.670 --> 11:29.410
They were nothing but knock-offs
made of scraps, after all.

11:29.410 --> 11:31.100
They were no match for us.

11:37.160 --> 11:38.250
They're here.

11:38.250 --> 11:39.590
Lots of them.

11:40.510 --> 11:41.340
Five of them.

11:41.760 --> 11:44.210
Wolf, I'll let you have them.

11:44.440 --> 11:46.050
No way. It's too much work.

11:46.050 --> 11:47.620
You do it, Lud-kun.

11:47.620 --> 11:49.130
You fussy boy.

11:49.130 --> 11:50.600
Then let us play rock-paper-scissors again.

11:50.600 --> 11:52.730
Foot rock-paper-scissors, then.

11:52.730 --> 11:53.960
Foot rock-paper-scissors?

11:53.960 --> 11:56.230
This is paper, and this is scissors.

11:56.500 --> 11:57.200
Stop.

11:57.200 --> 11:58.750
How is this scissors?

11:58.750 --> 12:00.170
Isn't it scissory?

12:00.170 --> 12:01.280
I'm not convinced.

12:01.280 --> 12:02.860
You're so fussy.

12:02.860 --> 12:05.790
Guys, we're keeping them waiting.

12:07.080 --> 12:08.700
Wh-What...

12:11.020 --> 12:13.320
Part of the amplifier is damaged.

12:13.320 --> 12:15.050
Main systems are holding up.

12:18.250 --> 12:20.000
Come on, look carefully.

12:19.180 --> 12:22.420
Wolf, don't make up rules just to suit yourself.

12:20.000 --> 12:20.920
See, scissors.

12:22.420 --> 12:25.720
Guys, we don't have time.

12:22.420 --> 12:25.720
Rock-paper-scissors is
meant to be played thus...

12:29.820 --> 12:30.470
Girl!

12:29.820 --> 12:30.470
Kanae!

12:37.440 --> 12:38.690
This Musik...

12:45.990 --> 12:47.260
Bach-san...

13:13.190 --> 13:15.010
That's all you ever do.

13:15.010 --> 13:16.320
What can you expect?

13:16.320 --> 13:18.050
She's got nothing else.

13:18.050 --> 13:19.240
One-hit wonder.

13:19.680 --> 13:21.230
Shut up!

13:28.990 --> 13:29.820
Why?

13:30.240 --> 13:31.830
Why, Bach-sama?

13:32.160 --> 13:36.080
You're the greatest ClassicaLoid
and the image of perfection.

13:36.400 --> 13:38.210
You don't need those jerks.

13:38.210 --> 13:41.310
You can make all humanity
one with your music.

13:41.310 --> 13:43.340
We can create an ideal world.

13:43.580 --> 13:46.290
That's why I made the MitsuruLoids.

13:49.360 --> 13:51.770
You don't understand anything.

13:53.330 --> 13:56.740
Music cannot be but one color.

13:57.160 --> 14:01.020
Music is made when many sounds
mix and play off one another.

14:02.340 --> 14:07.740
It is not until the sound created
by the eight musical geniuses,

14:07.740 --> 14:09.740
whose music I've vetted,

14:09.740 --> 14:15.020
creates a scale, and a seamless tone is born
that will fill the world and change it.

14:16.470 --> 14:21.150
That is why I have been waiting
for the other seven to awaken.

14:21.150 --> 14:21.910
Is this it?

14:21.910 --> 14:22.990
It's so big.

14:22.990 --> 14:23.780
Huh?

14:23.780 --> 14:24.670
Is it broken?

14:25.230 --> 14:28.480
And now, the time has come.

14:36.640 --> 14:38.710
Shall we not make a new world...

14:38.710 --> 14:43.190
A world in which music can
exist purely as music?

14:43.190 --> 14:43.890
I refuse.

14:43.890 --> 14:44.940
Nope.

14:45.440 --> 14:46.570
I see.

14:47.340 --> 14:50.030
In that case, I'll have
to force you to submit.

14:56.720 --> 14:58.870
There really is no end to them.

14:58.870 --> 15:01.580
They're going to wear us down.

15:08.230 --> 15:11.650
You're musicians. You must feel it...

15:11.650 --> 15:15.140
How twisted the music of this world is.

15:15.750 --> 15:19.390
Consumed like water, treated as disposables.

15:20.060 --> 15:28.150
People seek music as background,
as incidental, as messaging.

15:28.930 --> 15:33.240
So-called "musicians" do
not give birth to music.

15:33.670 --> 15:36.240
Rather, they take orders, and
itemize and assemble the sounds

15:36.240 --> 15:38.250
that are asked of them,
to be packaged and presented.

15:38.250 --> 15:41.920
Unfortunately, that has been
true both now and before.

15:43.290 --> 15:47.030
Do you not want to change this world?

15:48.170 --> 15:49.280
Not at all.

15:49.280 --> 15:50.130
Nope.

15:50.130 --> 15:50.880
Why?

15:51.590 --> 15:54.170
I don't care what anyone asks of me.

15:54.170 --> 15:57.510
I'll make music as my passion compels me to.

15:57.750 --> 15:59.460
Just do what you feel like.

15:59.460 --> 16:02.480
Bam, boom, freedom!

16:04.670 --> 16:07.470
Have I not told you that
appetite and selfishness

16:07.470 --> 16:09.360
are not the same as passion or freedom?

16:11.090 --> 16:14.820
Do you not realize that
you are already changing?

16:17.430 --> 16:20.580
You have a hall that you cherish.

16:21.230 --> 16:23.170
You have friends with whom to make music.

16:23.940 --> 16:27.040
You have a distinguished conductor
who waves her baton with fire.

16:27.760 --> 16:32.910
You create music every day to
conserve your modest recital group.

16:34.450 --> 16:35.660
Waving her baton?

16:35.660 --> 16:37.510
A distinguished conductor?

16:39.400 --> 16:41.570
That is the nature of the musician.

16:42.070 --> 16:46.400
A musician creates the best music they
can, in pursuit of their unwavering goal.

16:47.270 --> 16:51.690
Amidst lonely freedom and fortunate
difficulties, they struggle,

16:51.690 --> 16:54.280
they agonize, and they suffer.

16:55.420 --> 17:00.520
The world I seek is one where
we are free from that suffering.

17:01.550 --> 17:02.580
So...

17:02.860 --> 17:06.080
What kind of world do you
intend to make, Bach-san?

17:07.240 --> 17:10.090
A world in which everything
is rooted in music.

17:10.550 --> 17:14.180
There, everyone becomes a ClassicaLoid.

17:14.180 --> 17:16.260
Music becomes the universal language.

17:17.020 --> 17:21.100
Through music, people speak, laugh, and live.

17:21.530 --> 17:23.770
Music becomes humanity itself.

17:24.780 --> 17:26.650
Music ceases to be something special,

17:27.420 --> 17:30.190
but instead fills the world
like the air we breathe.

17:31.680 --> 17:33.150
Ceases to be something special?

17:33.470 --> 17:37.320
Do you not want to see such a world?

17:38.490 --> 17:39.520
Nope.

17:39.520 --> 17:40.330
Not at all.

17:40.540 --> 17:41.240
Why?

17:41.580 --> 17:44.250
You! Have you ever had gyoza?

17:45.100 --> 17:46.000
What?

17:46.290 --> 17:49.500
When I make gyoza, I forget about music.

17:49.500 --> 17:52.090
For I commit the entirety
of my mind and spirit

17:52.090 --> 17:54.370
to the creation of the harmony
of meat, vegetable, and wrapper.

17:54.370 --> 17:57.170
And when I taste a
perfectly-fried masterpiece,

17:57.170 --> 17:59.320
I can't help but want to play music.

17:59.320 --> 18:00.620
<i>That</i> is music.

18:00.620 --> 18:04.140
Why must we be forced to do music
with neither reason nor ceremony?

18:04.530 --> 18:05.860
He's right.

18:05.860 --> 18:11.270
Music comes to my mind naturally when I
have plenty of laughs with cute girls.

18:11.270 --> 18:14.640
Dude, would you even have fun
listening to music all the time?

18:14.640 --> 18:15.570
Are you serious?

18:16.360 --> 18:17.660
You fools.

18:17.660 --> 18:20.820
You <i>wish</i> to stay in an imperfect world?

18:21.540 --> 18:25.390
If we could speak through music, there would be
neither miscommunication nor misunderstanding.

18:25.390 --> 18:29.330
Not with any kind of person, nor
even with any kind of animal.

18:29.760 --> 18:32.500
Not even with the inhabitants
of other worlds.

18:32.500 --> 18:34.710
We could have understanding with <i>everyone</i>.

18:34.710 --> 18:35.920
Silence.

18:35.920 --> 18:38.550
I have only one thing to say to you.

18:39.640 --> 18:42.390
Get off your high horse!

18:43.970 --> 18:46.190
Oh, and one more thing.

18:47.600 --> 18:50.690
Tootie-toot!

18:54.240 --> 18:56.190
I will say no more.

19:04.440 --> 19:07.080
That might be lonely, though.

19:08.840 --> 19:12.220
I have old records at my place.

19:12.220 --> 19:14.170
My grandmother loved records.

19:15.520 --> 19:20.300
Whenever anything good happened,
she would play them for me.

19:20.830 --> 19:23.800
I loved those moments.

19:24.770 --> 19:29.220
Even now, when I hear those pieces,
I think of Grandma's smile.

19:30.320 --> 19:34.570
Not just her face, but
her scent and her voice.

19:35.440 --> 19:38.710
Special music for special days.

19:40.250 --> 19:42.980
Music doesn't exist everywhere.

19:42.980 --> 19:45.180
Maybe that's why it's special.

19:45.720 --> 19:49.750
It might be a bit sad if it became normal.

19:50.980 --> 19:53.040
My grandmother's memories...

19:53.040 --> 19:57.000
No, all kinds of music.

19:57.000 --> 20:00.340
Everything comes with special memories.

20:02.020 --> 20:03.150
Memories...

20:18.910 --> 20:19.690
I...

20:22.210 --> 20:24.280
Spielen wir unsere...

20:24.280 --> 20:26.200
Fühle meine...

20:26.200 --> 20:28.840
Musik!

21:07.950 --> 21:08.910
Huh?

21:09.730 --> 21:10.620
I...

21:10.910 --> 21:12.750
What? Why...

21:12.750 --> 21:15.250
It looks like Bach's music stopped.

21:21.480 --> 21:23.510
Hey, it's over.

21:24.120 --> 21:26.770
That's my daughter.

21:31.720 --> 21:33.300
Hey, are you sure about this?

21:33.300 --> 21:35.580
We didn't overdo it, did we?

21:35.580 --> 21:38.120
What if he charges us for repairs?

21:38.120 --> 21:40.160
Indeed, you've gone too far, Wolf.

21:40.160 --> 21:41.530
That was you, Lud-kun.

21:41.530 --> 21:42.540
I had no choice.

21:42.540 --> 21:44.300
The girl told me to.

21:44.300 --> 21:46.280
Kanae's savage.

21:47.070 --> 21:47.810
Say what?

21:47.810 --> 21:48.510
That was you two.

21:48.520 --> 21:49.880
Relax.

21:50.610 --> 21:51.880
Bach-sama.

21:51.880 --> 21:53.100
He's alive.

21:53.100 --> 21:54.120
Umm...

21:54.120 --> 21:57.290
So you mean to say you aren't
going to charge us, right?

21:57.820 --> 21:58.530
Right?!

22:02.420 --> 22:05.720
I just can't get along with you.

22:07.090 --> 22:08.510
Nor can I.

22:08.510 --> 22:11.330
You're surprisingly goofy, though, Bach.

22:11.330 --> 22:15.730
You were, like, "We could have understanding
even with the inhabitants of other worlds."

22:16.180 --> 22:17.690
Oh, yeah.

22:18.590 --> 22:20.090
What's up with that?

22:20.090 --> 22:22.030
Do you mean, like, aliens?

22:35.400 --> 22:37.500
It's upon us.

24:15.970 --> 24:30.990
Encore from the Skies

24:19.200 --> 24:20.000
You're kidding.

24:20.000 --> 24:20.930
Aliens?

24:20.930 --> 24:22.660
They came to Earth for our Musik?

24:22.660 --> 24:23.440
Why?

24:23.440 --> 24:24.510
Their reasons are unknown.

24:24.510 --> 24:25.890
But it's certainly a crisis.

24:25.890 --> 24:28.710
Literally, an existential
crisis for humanity.
